Q: how to find number pattern in a string A: <p>You can use a regular expression that just matches digits, since the number you want is the only digits in the string.</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-js lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>let strings = ["ColorSlice1MouseOver",
  "ColorSlice1MouseOver",
  "ColorSlice12MouseOver",
  "ColorSlice32MouseOver"
];
strings.forEach(str =&gt; {
  let match = str.match(/\d+/);
  if (match) {
    console.log(`${str} =&gt; ${match[0]}`);
  }
});</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>
